      "title": "Russia to take 70K Indian skilled workers this year: Govt tells Parl panel",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/russia-to-take-70k-indian-skilled-workers-this-year-govt-tells-parl-panel-126100300946_1.html",
      "description": "External Affairs Minister S Jaishankar on Saturday briefed a parliamentary consultative committee on India's \"multifaceted\" engagement with Russia, highlighting shared ambitions to expand bilateral trade, investment, and energy cooperation.\nChairing the meeting on India-Russia relations, Jaishankar also apprised members of New Delhi's stance on the Ukraine conflict and its recent diplomatic efforts to contribute toward a peaceful settlement.\nThe external affairs minister further informed the panel that Russia has agreed to take around 70,000 Indian skilled workers this year, especially in the fields of construction and logistics, people familiar with the meeting said.\nWhile discussing the trade and investment ties between the two countries, Jaishankar mentioned that there is a shared ambition to expand bilateral trade in a balanced manner, including through greater Indian exports to Russia in seven areas -- auto, pharma, food, marine products, engineering goods, chemicals and ...",
